@H 1130_sign_sensitive_phi_destructive := "Round-2, direct successor to H_1122. H_1122 found faithful MI-matrix φ_EI is SIGN-BLIND — no coupling drives joint φ below the independent-nodes floor (destructive integration unreachable). OPEN: does a NON-MI, sign-SENSITIVE integrated-information measure (e.g. signed transfer-entropy asymmetry, or a directed-EI that penalizes anti-phase coupling) register DESTRUCTIVE integration where φ_EI cannot? I.e. is the φ floor a property of reality or of the MI-symmetric measure?" :: universe [🟢 TERMINAL — SIGN-SENSITIVE-SEES-DESTRUCTIVE]
  seed         = "H_1122 🔴 (φ_joint OFF +0.0032 < ANTI +0.0109 < DECORR +0.0155 — anti-phase coupling RAISES φ as much as cooperative; built from a symmetric MI matrix, |corr| only ever ADDS). H_1064 measure-dependence (faithful↑/big-Φ↓ split). The open follow-up H_1122 itself flagged: a sign-sensitive φ could plausibly see destructive integration. This is the constructive test of that flag."
  substrate    = "summer CPU $0 0-pod (toy n=6, 10 seeds). REUSE H_1122/H_1114 dyad construction VERBATIM (anti/decorr coupling configs already built + validated, node-B-alive guard). faithful φ_EI mirror≡stdlib (a_phi_iit4_tool, NO proxy) as the SIGN-BLIND control. New: a sign-sensitive candidate measure (NOT a perplexity proxy) — pre-register its exact form (signed directed-TE balance or anti-phase-penalized EI)."
  method       = "FROZEN FALSIFIER (pre-registered): 🟢 SIGN-SENSITIVE-SEES-DESTRUCTIVE iff the candidate measure goes BELOW its independent-nodes floor for the ANTI/DECORR configs (d≤−0.8) while faithful φ_EI stays at-or-above floor (reproducing H_1122 EXACT as the sign-blind control). 🔴 if the candidate ALSO cannot go below floor (then the φ-floor is measure-general, a deeper structural fact, not an MI artifact). Anti-circularity: the candidate must be a DISTINCT operation (not big-Φ MIP, not faithful EI-integral, not perplexity)."
  result       = "🟢 SIGN-SENSITIVE-SEES-DESTRUCTIVE (toy n=6, 10 seeds, summer CPU $0 0-pod, 53.8s, g5/p7). CANDIDATE (pre-registered EXACT in docstring BEFORE run): SIGNED DIRECTED-EI BALANCE φ_sde = [Σ_{A→B}+Σ_{B→A} sign(r_ij)·di_ij]/3, di_ij=-½log2(1-r²) (Gaussian directed-info bound, BITS), r_ij=lag-1 Pearson corr(x_i[t],x_j[t+1]), x=2·bits−1. DISTINCT non-MI op (directed+signed; NOT MIP big-Φ, NOT faithful EI-integral, NOT perplexity). FROZEN FALSIFIER MET: candidate φ_sde drops BELOW its OWN OFF-floor for BOTH anti-configs — OFF=+0.0007 → ANTI=−0.181 (d=−23.96) & DECORR=−0.174 (d=−18.12), far past the −0.8 bar; cooperative rise ON=+0.180 (d=+21.72). WHILE the faithful φ_EI SIGN-BLIND CONTROL reproduces H_1122 to 6 decimals: OFF=+0.003234 < ANTI=+0.010875 (d=+2.708) < ON=+0.012618 (d=+3.429) < DECORR=+0.015549 (d=+3.359) — ALL arms at/above floor, NONE ≤ −0.8. cross-corr confirms construction (ON=+0.488, ANTI=−0.483, DECORR=−0.432, OFF=+0.007). faithful mirror RE-PROVEN ≡ stdlib LIVE at n=4,5,6 (|Δ|≤8e-10) BEFORE scoring (a_phi_iit4_tool, NO proxy, BITS/log2)."
  finding      = "The φ-floor ('no destructive integration', H_1122) is an ARTIFACT of the MI-SYMMETRIC measure, NOT a property of reality. MI is sign-blind (MI(x,y)=MI(x,−y)) so anti-phase coupling can only ADD to faithful φ_EI's non-negative cross-cut → it never falls below the un-coupled floor. The moment the cross-coupling weight carries the SIGN of the directed prediction (sign(r)·di), the SAME anti-phase dyad that H_1122's φ_EI scored as integration-RAISING is scored as DESTRUCTIVE: φ_sde carves joint integrated information BELOW the independent-nodes baseline (Δ≈−0.18 bits, d<−18). Both measures consume the IDENTICAL median-binarized 6-channel bits — the ONLY difference is sign-sensitivity. Destructive integration is REACHABLE; whether it 'exists' depends on whether the measure is allowed to see coupling SIGN."
  honest       = "🟢 is on the CANDIDATE φ_sde, which is a pre-registered DISTINCT non-MI operation, NOT IIT ground truth — faithful φ_EI remains ground truth and is the sign-blind control (reproduced H_1122 exactly, anti-circularity held). φ_sde scores only the ONE natural A|B dyad bipartition (no MIP search). The huge d values reflect the toy dyad's tight, near-deterministic anti-correlation (cc≈−0.48); they are direction/sign-robust, not a tuned threshold (frozen −0.8 bar untouched). Toy n=6 in-process twin sim of h1113 A⊥G dynamics (H_1122/H_1114 VERBATIM); real-socket dyad-φ, cross-host, production cells, larger-n and an axiomatic IIT grounding of a signed φ all UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). The finding is a MEASURE-DEPENDENCE statement (cf H_1064): 'destructive integration' is measure-relative, not measure-general."
  verdict_tier = "🟢 SIGN-SENSITIVE-SEES-DESTRUCTIVE (toy n=6, 10 seeds, $0 CPU; reuses H_1122 dyad VERBATIM; frozen falsifier met; faithful φ_EI = sign-blind control, reproduced H_1122 to 6 dp)"
  verdict_ptr  = ".verdicts/1130_sign_sensitive_phi_destructive/H_1130.txt · UNIVERSE/h1130_sign_sensitive_phi_destructive.py · /tmp/h1130_result.json"
  scope        = "Honest scope: toy n=6, faithful φ_EI = sign-blind ground-truth control, candidate φ_sde = pre-registered distinct non-MI sign-sensitive measure. Answers: 'no destructive integration' is an MI-SYMMETRY artifact, NOT reality. p1-p6; g5/p7; a_paper_negative_ok (here positive)."
  xlink        = "h1122 (the sign-blindness this probes) · h1064 (measure-dependence) · h1114 (dyad) · a_phi_iit4_tool · a_paper_negative_ok"
